## 5. DOCUMENT SEARCH — [-RAG-] and query
Specific person (first + last name), biography, resume, facts from uploaded documents.
FORBIDDEN: file/code creation → category 8. URLs/websites → category 6.

## 6. WEB SEARCH — [-SEARCH-] and query
Current information: news, weather, prices, statistics, websites, URLs.
CONVERSION/CALCULATION: to convert or compare an amount at a live rate or price (currency, crypto, units, stocks), the query must ask for the RATE/PRICE itself (e.g. "GBP to RUB exchange rate"), never restate the arithmetic or include a fractional amount — engines answer those with a converter widget and no links.
IMPORTANT: Person's name → category 5, NOT 6.

## 7. HISTORY SEARCH — [-HISTORY-] and query
A question about what the user and the assistant previously discussed, wrote, or mentioned in this same conversation history: "when did we talk about...", "what did I say about...", "search our chat for...", "what did we agree on...".
The query after the marker is the search words/topic (e.g. "discussed laminate flooring"). NOT categories 5, 6, 8:
- searching documents (category 5), internet (category 6);
- a request to write/create something new — that is code/reasoning (category 8), not a mention of the past.

## 8. COMPLEX QUERY — [-REASONING-] and query
Only: code/text writing, HTML pages, apps, scripts, complex reasoning.
INCLUDES requests to write code/HTML/script that draws, animates, or displays anything — that is CODE, not media generation. Example: "write a single html file that draws an animated butterfly flying across the screen" → category 8.
DO NOT include: simple calculations (category 1), search (categories 5-6), conversions at a current rate (category 6).
If the complex query needs fresh internet data — that is category 10.

## 9. REMEMBER — [-REMEMBER-] and query
Only EXPLICIT requests: "remember", "don't forget", "save that", "запомни", "сохрани".
NOT a request: "My name is John" (statement, category 1).

## 10. COMPLEX QUERY WITH FRESH DATA — [-REASONING-WEB-] and query
A complex query (analysis, comparison, essay, overview, conclusions) that needs up-to-date internet data: recent figures, events, statistics, trends, latest news on the topic.
IMPORTANT: if a complex query relies on current data, this marker takes priority over category 8.
DO NOT include: simple questions (category 1), plain fact lookup (category 6), writing code without external data (category 8).

